 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Cells Annotation\n",
    "\n",
    "Cell type classification was carried out using the *SCSA* tool [1].\n",
    "\n",
    "All the information about downloading, installation, and usage of *SCSA* can be found [here](https://github.com/bioinfo-ibms-pumc/SCSA).\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "[1] Cao Y, Wang X, and Peng G (2020) SCSA: A Cell Type Annotation Tool for Single-Cell RNA-seq Data. *Front. Genet.*, 11:490. [doi:10.3389/fgene.2020.00490](https://doi.org/10.3389/fgene.2020.00490)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Import SCSA"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import scanpy as sc\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "After cloning the git repository SCSA, choose the folder SCSA as directory."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "cd SCSA"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We are ready to run the scsa.py file. Let's look at the help."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "usage: SCSA.py [-h] -i INPUT [-o OUTPUT] [-d DB] [-s SOURCE] [-c CLUSTER]\n",
      "               [-M MARKERDB] [-f FOLDCHANGE] [-p PVALUE] [-w WEIGHT]\n",
      "               [-g SPECIES] [-k TISSUE] [-m OUTFMT] [-T CELLTYPE] [-t TARGET]\n",
      "               [-E] [-N] [-b] [-l]\n",
      "\n",
      "Program: SCSA\n",
      "  Version: 1.0\n",
      "  Email  : <yhcao@ibms.pumc.edu.cn>\n",
      "        \n",
      "\n",
      "options:\n",
      "  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n",
      "  -i INPUT, --input INPUT\n",
      "                        Input file for marker annotation(Only CSV format\n",
      "                        supported).\n",
      "  -o OUTPUT, --output OUTPUT\n",
      "                        Output file for marker annotation.\n",
      "  -d DB, --db DB        Database for annotation. (whole.db)\n",
      "  -s SOURCE, --source SOURCE\n",
      "                        Source of marker genes.\n",
      "                        (cellranger,[seurat],[scanpy],[scran])\n",
      "  -c CLUSTER, --cluster CLUSTER\n",
      "                        Only deal with one cluster of marker genes.\n",
      "                        (all,[1],[1,2,3],[...])\n",
      "  -M MARKERDB, --MarkerDB MARKERDB\n",
      "                        User-defined marker database in table format with two\n",
      "                        columns.First column as Cellname, Second refers to\n",
      "                        Genename.\n",
      "  -f FOLDCHANGE, --foldchange FOLDCHANGE\n",
      "                        Fold change threshold for marker filtering. (2.0)\n",
      "  -p PVALUE, --pvalue PVALUE\n",
      "                        P-value threshold for marker filtering. (0.05)\n",
      "  -w WEIGHT, --weight WEIGHT\n",
      "                        Weight threshold for marker filtering from cellranger\n",
      "                        v1.0 results. (100)\n",
      "  -g SPECIES, --species SPECIES\n",
      "                        Species for annotation. Only used for cellmarker\n",
      "                        database. ('Human',['Mouse'])\n",
      "  -k TISSUE, --tissue TISSUE\n",
      "                        Tissue for annotation. Only used for cellmarker\n",
      "                        database. Multiple tissues should be seperated by\n",
      "                        commas. Run '-l' option to see all tissues.\n",
      "                        ('All',['Bone marrow'],['Bone\n",
      "                        marrow,Brain,Blood'][...])\n",
      "  -m OUTFMT, --outfmt OUTFMT\n",
      "                        Output file format for marker annotation. (ms-\n",
      "                        excel,[txt])\n",
      "  -T CELLTYPE, --celltype CELLTYPE\n",
      "                        Cell type for annotation. (normal,[cancer])\n",
      "  -t TARGET, --target TARGET\n",
      "                        Target to annotation class in Database.\n",
      "                        (cellmarker,[cancersea])\n",
      "  -E, --Gensymbol       Using gene symbol ID instead of ensembl ID in input\n",
      "                        file for calculation.\n",
      "  -N, --norefdb         Only using user-defined marker database for\n",
      "                        annotation.\n",
      "  -b, --noprint         Do not print any detail results.\n",
      "  -l, --list_tissue     List tissue names in database.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "!python SCSA.py -h"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Run scsa.py\n",
    "\n",
    "Run `scsa.py` by providing the Scanpy result CSV file as input and defining other inputs accordingly. \n",
    "\n",
    "Remember to:\n",
    "- Set an appropriate Log Fold Change (LFC) threshold.\n",
    "- Set an appropriate p-value threshold.\n",
    "- Upload the Scanpy results CSV file.\n",
    "- Write the annotation results to a `.txt` file.\n"
   ]
  },
